                ],
                "evidence": "The LatticeCache 2.3 Pro plan costs **$45/month**. That includes 20 GB of storage, 50M reads and 10M writes per month. The **max item size is 5 MB**.\n\n**Included in the $45/month base price:**\n- 20 GB of replicated NVMe cache storage\n- 50 million read ops/month\n- 10 million write ops/month\n\n**Overage rates once you go past those amounts:**\n| Resource | Overage rate |\n|---|---|\n| Storage | $1.80 per extra GB-month |\n| Reads | $0.12 per extra million ops |\n| Writes | $0.60 per extra million ops |\n\n**Hard limits in 2.3:**\n- Max size of a single item (value): **5 MB**\n- Max key length: 1,024 bytes\n- Max concurrent client connections per cache namespace: 2,000\n\nAs an example I worked out myself (not from the source), a month with 25 GB stored, 80M reads and 12M writes would cost about $45 + $9 (storage) + $3.60 (reads) + $1.20 (writes) ≈ **$58.80**.\n\n**Source:** this all comes from the vault page [[LatticeCache]] (`wiki/LatticeCache.md`). It was taken from LatticeCache's official pricing and limits page (updated 2026-11-02) and checked on 2026-11-04. The page is 3 days old, which is well within its 30-day freshness window, so I didn't check the web again.\n\nCoverage: vault only (one page). No web searches, because the vault answered the question while still current. Social lane not searched since this is a single fact. No paid calls."
